{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>I stood between YHWH and between you.</b> I have explained it." "<b>For you were afraid of the fire.</b> And if you did not ascend the mountain." "And the word <b>לאמר</b> (saying) is attached to the matter: \"YHWH spoke with you on the mountain from the midst of the fire, לאמר.\" And it is possible for the interpretation of \"I stood between YHWH\" to be after the standing at Mount Sinai, and the meaning is that He spoke with you face to face, and from that day I was standing between YHWH and between you, for you were afraid, as will be explained." "<b>And you did not ascend the mountain.</b> As I ascended, I and Moses drew near to the cloud. And do not set your mind to it because the word לאמר is distant, for many are so, and the Speaker did not interrupt the verses nor the sections. Also do not set your mind to the words, for they are like bodies and the meanings like spirits, and the cutting is with both implements — this like that — in the act, it is a single act. Therefore שוא (emptiness) and שקר (falsehood), for they are brothers, and every שקר is שוא. And I have already explained that זכור (remember) is like שמור (observe). And He added \"as YHWH your Elohim commanded you,\" and the meaning is at the standing at Mount Sinai."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {3 "The text 'ומשה נגש' reads hyper-literally as 'and Moses drew near'; the subject of 'עליתי אני' (I ascended) is Moses, who then says 'and Moses drew near' in third person, which is awkward but preserved as-is."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:22:28.907582701Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}